                "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                "word": "mistrustful",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "37af21ca-f643-42a0-be89-e88fa7b916bd",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more mistrustful"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3d41a4db-2f48-4093-b338-024f0d6fb35c",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most mistrustful"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6038c0fd-9b87-3846-85a0-5cb1fac41321",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having mistrust, lacking trust (in someone or something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1de7abfc-4ce9-44ec-91c5-1a955c3635fb",
                                "sense_id": "6038c0fd-9b87-3846-85a0-5cb1fac41321",
                                "text": "[…] I hold it cowardice\nTo rest mistrustful where a noble heart\nHath pawn’d an open hand in sign of love;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8608ba8a-9d22-40e6-b559-12f1a6dd40fa",
                                "sense_id": "6038c0fd-9b87-3846-85a0-5cb1fac41321",
                                "text": "In the passage I met the nurse. She greeted me with a little smile; but I was mistrustful of professional cheerfulness that night."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "026e49e1-d6c0-37cb-af31-5ecc3eb65a73",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Expressing or showing a lack of trust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04659fe8-7d36-401f-8ef4-0330e155255d",
                                "sense_id": "026e49e1-d6c0-37cb-af31-5ecc3eb65a73",
                                "text": "He lookt askew with his mistrustfull eyes,\nAnd nycely trode, as thornes lay in his way"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ef3f366-46ca-4bfa-82dd-9092d90fd3a1",
                                "sense_id": "026e49e1-d6c0-37cb-af31-5ecc3eb65a73",
                                "text": "At last, having held a document before her glasses for nearly five minutes, she presented it across the counter; accompanying the act by another inquisitive and mistrustful glance—it was for J. E."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "904b3801-c708-48f6-8e37-a52f560a51d1",
                                "sense_id": "026e49e1-d6c0-37cb-af31-5ecc3eb65a73",
                                "text": "He led the way to the stable-yard accordingly, the Rat following with a most mistrustful expression […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d799179a-8a07-35a5-bb67-3f7c1f0b13a9",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a suspicion, imagining or supposing (that something undesirable is the case)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f8e5f42-3993-406e-8c9d-edf1b780f5eb",
                                "sense_id": "d799179a-8a07-35a5-bb67-3f7c1f0b13a9",
                                "text": "The mender of roads was now coming to himself, and was mistrustful of having made a mistake in his late demonstrations; but no."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96ca49e7-2f9a-31de-836d-180dc19efaea",
                        "entry_id": "f21337dc-c867-347c-aab9-c0fdbbbcb27c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing mistrust, suspicions, or forebodings."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "326b94a6-a9dd-4e2c-80e4-5cb8fe5b91c4",
                                "sense_id": "96ca49e7-2f9a-31de-836d-180dc19efaea",
                                "text": "Vp we gad, owt spredding oure sayls and make to the seaward:\nAl creeks mistrustful with Greekish countrye refusing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9915ba6-c602-48a2-a811-a60e8958c256",
                                "sense_id": "96ca49e7-2f9a-31de-836d-180dc19efaea",
                                "text": "[…] stonish’d as night-wanderers often are,\nTheir light blown out in some mistrustful wood,\nEven so confounded in the dark she lay,\nHaving lost the fair discovery of her way."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
